WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.230
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Joanna] Every time you go through

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.720
this Hardee's Drive-through, you'll hear

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.553
- [Automated Message]
Would you like to try

00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:07.290
a peach pie for 1.59?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.123
- Nope.

00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:08.956
- [Automated Message]
Would you like to try

00:00:08.956 --> 00:00:10.139
a peach pie for 1.59?

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:10.972
- No.

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:12.360
- [Automated Message] Peach pie for 1.59?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.193
- No, thank you.

00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:14.040
- [Automated Message] Peach pie?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.189
- No peach pie.

00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:16.350
- [Automated Message]
I have one peach pie.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.490
- No peach pie.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.500
That's because that's an AI chatbot

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.287
that now takes all the
drive-through orders

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.960
at this Hardee's location
on Kent Island, in Maryland.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.507
Well, unless the bot needs human help.

00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:28.380
- [Automated Message] One moment.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.742
Let me get a team member to help you.

00:00:29.742 --> 00:00:31.860
- [Hardee's Employee]
Sorry, how may I help you?

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.693
- [Joanna] And this tech

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:34.740
may be coming to a restaurant near you.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.420
Made by a company named Presto,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.443
it's available at 350
locations in the country,

00:00:39.443 --> 00:00:43.110
including Carl's Jr.,
Del Taco, and Checkers.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.650
It even uses some of OpenAI's GPT tech.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.180
But, how does the tech work?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.013
And is it really taking over real jobs?

00:00:51.013 --> 00:00:51.846
- We don't need that, right?

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:53.035
- I designed three challenges

00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:56.553
and drove through this
drive-through about 30 times

00:00:56.553 --> 00:00:57.746
(energetic music)

00:00:57.746 --> 00:00:59.005
- [Automated Message] Thank
you for choosing Hardee's.

00:00:59.005 --> 00:00:59.838
Thank you for choosing Hardee's.

00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:00.671
Thank you for choosing Hardee's.

00:01:00.671 --> 00:01:01.504
Thank you for choosing Hardee's.

00:01:01.504 --> 00:01:06.330
- to find out how good this bot
is at feeding hungry humans.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.240
Challenge one, speech recognition.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.710
The first thing Presto does

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.780
is use automatic speech recognition

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.820
to convert an order to text,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.640
so the AI system can understand it.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.754
I'd like the Big Hardee Combo

00:01:19.754 --> 00:01:22.057
with extra ketchup and a Diet Coke.

00:01:22.057 --> 00:01:22.950
- [Automated Message] Sure.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.954
Would you like to make
that a medium or a large?

00:01:24.954 --> 00:01:25.920
- [Joanna] But as we all know

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.960
from speech to text on our phones,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.090
sometimes it isn't perfect,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.505
especially with background noise,

00:01:31.505 --> 00:01:32.338
(car horn)

00:01:32.338 --> 00:01:34.980
which there's typically a
lot of at a drive through.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.232
Initiate dog sounds.

00:01:37.232 --> 00:01:39.754
Can I get the 10 piece chicken nuggets?

00:01:39.754 --> 00:01:40.587
(dog barking)

00:01:40.587 --> 00:01:42.224
- [Automated Message] What
dipping sauce would you like?

00:01:42.224 --> 00:01:43.246
(dog barking)

00:01:43.246 --> 00:01:44.137
- What dipping sauces do you have?

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.583
- [Automated Message] Ranch,
honey mustard, barbecue sauce,

00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.184
honey-q, and hot or creamy Buffalo sauce.

00:01:49.184 --> 00:01:51.431
- I'll do the honey mustard.

00:01:51.431 --> 00:01:52.362
Do you like dogs?

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:53.462
(dog barking)

00:01:53.462 --> 00:01:55.172
- [Automated Message] Sure.

00:01:55.172 --> 00:01:57.662
- [Joanna] Okay, but what about,

00:01:57.662 --> 00:01:59.331
can I get a kid's meal?

00:01:59.331 --> 00:02:00.164
- [Automated Message] Got it.

00:02:00.164 --> 00:02:00.997
(child crying)

00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:03.223
- Let's do the two-piece chicken tenders.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.884
- [Automated Message] What
dipping sauce would you like?

00:02:04.884 --> 00:02:05.880
(child crying)

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.926
- [Joanna] And for the extreme challenge.

00:02:07.926 --> 00:02:09.725
- [Automated Message] What can
we get started for you today?

00:02:09.725 --> 00:02:10.784
(car horn)

00:02:10.784 --> 00:02:12.633
- Can I get a Big Hardee with a Diet Coke?

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.923
(car horn)

00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:16.096
- [Automated Message] Can
you please speak louder

00:02:16.096 --> 00:02:17.274
so that I may hear you?

00:02:17.274 --> 00:02:18.107
(car horn)

00:02:18.107 --> 00:02:20.087
- Just one Big Hardee
with a Diet Coke, please.

00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:20.940
- [Automated Message] One moment.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.010
Let me get a team member to help you.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.120
- [Joanna] Okay, I'm not even sure

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.830
a human would hear me over that.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.990
Challenge one, pass.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.230
Challenge two, natural
language processing.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.390
Once the system has that text prompt,

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:34.980
it goes to the AI brain,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.340
what's called Presto Natural
Language Understanding.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.170
The AI interprets the prompt

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.007
and determines a follow-up response.

00:02:42.007 --> 00:02:42.900
- [Automated Message] Would you like

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.850
to make that a medium or a large?

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:45.683
- Large.

00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:46.516
- [Automated Message]
Would you like to try

00:02:46.516 --> 00:02:47.970
a peach pie for 1.59?

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.290
What drink would you like?

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.110
- Diet Coke, and no to the peach pie.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.100
At this location,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.970
Presto has now incorporated
OpenAI's GPT into the system

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.890
to make the read back portion of the order

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.736
sound more human-like.

00:03:00.736 --> 00:03:01.740
- [Automated Message]
I have one number four,

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.700
the Big Hardee Combo

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.390
with extra ketchup, large
fries and a large diet Coke.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.659
Correct?

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:08.400
- [Joanna] Once the order is received,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.040
it's transferred to the
restaurant's kitchen display

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.890
so a human can make and
package up the food.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.597
For simple, straightforward
orders, it works well.

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:20.280
Got the order right.
It's fairly efficient.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.207
And yes, there's the upsell.

00:03:22.207 --> 00:03:24.360
- [Automated Message] Would
you like to try a peach pie?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.799
- I do not want the peach pie.

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:26.632
- [Automated Message] Got it.

00:03:26.632 --> 00:03:29.310
- [Joanna] It also did quite
well when I changed my order.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.470
I'd like the Big Hardee Combo.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.303
Actually.

00:03:32.303 --> 00:03:33.977
- [Automated Message] Sure.
Would you like medium or large?

00:03:33.977 --> 00:03:34.890
- Sorry. Sorry.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.177
Actually, I'd like the
Superstar with cheese.

00:03:37.177 --> 00:03:38.220
- [Automated Message] Sure thing.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.300
- [Joanna] Unlike ChatGPT,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.400
which is trained on a
large language model,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.712
this system is trained
on a limited set of data,

00:03:43.712 --> 00:03:46.020
including the restaurant's menu.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.707
Can I get two spicy tuna rolls?

00:03:47.707 --> 00:03:49.170
- [Automated Message] I'm sorry,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.150
but that item is currently unavailable.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.813
- You have a pepperoni pizza?

00:03:52.813 --> 00:03:54.027
- [Automated Message] No.

00:03:54.027 --> 00:03:56.940
- [Joanna] And it does fail
at some pretty simple tasks.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.470
Do you know how many calories there are

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.007
in the Western Bacon Cheeseburger?

00:04:00.007 --> 00:04:01.170
- [Automated Message] One moment.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.880
Let me get a team member to help you.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.767
- I am allergic to gluten.
Is there gluten in that?

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.470
- [Automated Message] No.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.660
- There's definitely gluten in that bread.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.781
Can I speak to a human?

00:04:10.781 --> 00:04:12.030
- [Automated Message] One moment please.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.770
Let me get someone to help you.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.140
- Hi, I'm sorry about that.
We do have a lettuce wrap.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.700
- [Joanna] Presto said this was an error

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.320
and that any allergy questions

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.660
should trigger the bot to get a human.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.890
Challenge two,

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.040
I'm giving it a pass, because
it did get most orders right.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.070
But yes, it needs to work
on the allergy issue.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.437
Challenge three, humanness.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.466
One of the things I like
about drive-throughs,

00:04:33.466 --> 00:04:38.466
or I say I like about drive-throughs,
is talking to a human.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.960
What's your favorite Taylor Swift song?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.620
What's your favorite thing on the menu?

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:48.184
Say "order when ready" please
if you are free tonight.

00:04:48.184 --> 00:04:51.255
- [Automated Message]
Order when ready please.

00:04:51.255 --> 00:04:52.200
- Yeah.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.910
But 3.3 million Americans are
fast food or counter workers,

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.850
making this a very human-centric job.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.842
Do we really want AI taking this job?

00:05:02.842 --> 00:05:07.350
Yet here at the Hardee's on
this 15 mile island in Maryland,

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:11.160
AI hasn't taken jobs, at least not yet.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.500
- We put Presto in to support our team.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.030
They're currently understaffed,

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.910
as in most restaurants
currently in the area.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.020
Now that we have Presto,

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.600
our frontline personnel are
more free to do other things

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.790
like drop fries, assemble orders,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.930
tend to dining room guests,

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.880
make our hand dipped ice cream shakes.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.440
Make sure that quality assurance

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.706
in every level is to standard.

00:05:30.706 --> 00:05:34.590
We have no intention of cutting labor.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.180
- [Joanna] And I was happy to hear that,

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.090
given how very nice the
humans at the Hardee's were

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:42.010
and how unhuman like the bot was.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:43.530
Okay, thank you so much.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.363
- Have a great day.

00:05:44.363 --> 00:05:46.350
- So, what did we learn here today?

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.970
Well, that this AI is very good

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.366
at the basics of drive
through order taking.

00:05:50.366 --> 00:05:53.400
But like most applications
of AI right now,

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.480
this is a way to help humans
rather than fully replace them.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.977
A human still has to babysit this bot.

00:05:59.977 --> 00:06:01.740
- [Hardee's Employee] So
typically this is where

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.450
we would lock in and take over.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.137
- But all I did was order the Big Hardee.

00:06:05.137 --> 00:06:06.660
- [Hardee's Employee] Yeah.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.666
This is what we deal with
sometimes. I apologize.

00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:10.620
- [Joanna] But of course,

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.870
this tech is only going to get better.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.370
And more companies will give in

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.948
to making AI part of their workforce.

00:06:16.948 --> 00:06:19.020
Just like I gave in

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:23.820
to the peach pie on a hundred degree day.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.412
Some cream filling.

00:06:25.412 --> 00:06:28.245
(energetic music)

